WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.050
- Do you remember the
first place you performed?

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.579
What was your first thing you did?

00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:07.682
- Well, Willies my home,
Willies in Stillwater, Oklahoma.

00:00:07.682 --> 00:00:09.832
I went to school at
Oklahoma State University

00:00:09.832 --> 00:00:11.680
and went through graduation,

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.320
got my blank diploma, kinda thing,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.790
and then got the call that I'm
one hour short of graduatin'.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.000
So I had to go back up for,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.780
and I didn't have any money, whatsoever.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.170
So I went down to a place called Willies.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.540
A lady named Dolly, Bill
and Dolly was there.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.400
And Dolly says, "I'll give you a shot."

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.330
I played one night, and she
was so sweet to me, man.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.047
It was that night she
looked at me, and she goes,

00:00:31.047 --> 00:00:32.807
"You know I'm tryin' not to negotiate

00:00:32.807 --> 00:00:35.017
"against myself here on price," she goes,

00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:37.747
"but you're kinda good at this.

00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:39.071
"I mean, you're good at this."

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:39.904
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:39.904 --> 00:00:41.380
And that made all the difference to me.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.010
I was like, "Oh really? That's cool."

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.610
And it gave me the confidence-
- It instilled confidence yeah

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.443
- You betcha.

00:00:45.443 --> 00:00:46.276
And that's where it all began,

00:00:46.276 --> 00:00:47.367
and thanks to Dolly and thanks to Willies

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.590
and the great people that showed up there,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.280
even the ones that don't
remember being there,

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.020
'cause there was a lot of 'em.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.728
- The friends in low places?
- Exactly!

00:00:54.728 --> 00:00:55.570
(audience laughs and claps)

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.270
- I always wonder, do you keep in touch

00:00:58.270 --> 00:00:59.303
with anybody from back then?

00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:01.582
Like at Willies, or that
place, or in the band or-

00:01:01.582 --> 00:01:02.800
- Oh, we're all still together.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.250
So the guy that was the bartender

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.100
went on to be the production
manager for the whole tour.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.933
- [Kelly] What?!

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.020
- So he runs the stadium tour.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.810
He does everything, his
name's Brian Petree.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.070
And then, of course, Ty.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.600
You know, Ty's the guitar player.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.030
We were college roommates together.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.620
And so we're still out
here, Ty will be playing

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.300
here with us later tonight.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.400
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.404
- Yeah it's fun.

00:01:20.404 --> 00:01:23.310
- What was it like
playing in your dorm room?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.040
Like, playing in your dorm
room, is that crazy, y'all?

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.019
- It was dark.

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.099
(audience laughs)

00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:31.737
- I'm just loving that people
down the hallway were like

00:01:31.737 --> 00:01:32.720
"Shut up!"

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:34.788
and you ended up being Garth Brooks.

00:01:34.788 --> 00:01:36.050
(audience laughs)
- Exactly!

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:37.131
- I just love that.

00:01:37.131 --> 00:01:39.339
Was he crazy then, was he fun?

00:01:39.339 --> 00:01:41.670
- It was just all based on just two guys

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.700
that loved music, I think.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.060
To this day, we knew
how we felt about music.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.900
We just didn't know how everybody else

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.980
was gonna feel about it at the time.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.740
- And the only difference, I think now,

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.923
is I look like this and he still
looks like he's in college.

00:01:54.923 --> 00:01:56.700
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.287
- I look slightly different, as well.

